missing_entity.description:
The entity `{entity_id}` does not exist or is disabled in Home Assistant, but is referenced by these Ambience scenes in the {scope}:
{scenes}

A condition referencing it will never match; an action targeting it will fail silently. Fix the entity id in the Ambience editor, enable the entity (or its device), or remove the reference. This message clears automatically once the entity exists and is enabled.

action_overlap.description:
The entity `{entity_id}` is controlled by more than one Ambience category/scope group:
{groups}

Each group is an independent control loop with its own state, so they can fight over this entity and produce stale or no-op applies. Consider moving it into a single group. This message clears automatically once the overlap is resolved.

missing_workday_sensor.description:
These Ambience scenes use a `workday` or `holiday` day-item, but no **workday sensor** is configured (Settings → Ambience → Conditions → Day), so they can never match:
{scenes}

Configure a workday sensor, or remove the workday/holiday items. This message clears automatically once it's resolved.

missing_workday_calendar.description:
These Ambience scenes use a `first_workday`/`last_workday` day-item, but no **workday calendar** is configured (Settings → Ambience → Conditions → Day), so they can never match:
{scenes}

Configure a workday calendar, or remove those items. This message clears automatically once it's resolved.

missing_weather_entity.description:
These Ambience scenes use a weather condition, but no **weather entity** is configured (Settings → Ambience → Conditions → Weather), so they can never match:
{scenes}

Configure a weather entity, or remove the weather conditions. This message clears automatically once it's resolved.

missing_weather_group.description:
The weather group `{ref}` no longer exists, but is referenced by these Ambience scenes:
{scenes}

A condition referencing it will never match. Re-create the group or remove the reference. This message clears automatically once it's resolved.

